      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "There are some games where people play just to see numbers go up. This is a nice and very helpful request, but I wonder if someone trying to crash people would see this as a positive feedback loop for their actions.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-09-16T02:07:55.076Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Have you ever noticed users suddenly freezes? And have you ever wondered: are these lags or is the user just distracted by something? Can user see me? Can I be sure they can hear what I am saying? Did they saw what I did? It was lag on my side, or on other's?\nOr maybe... You were talking to another player, but suddenly there was a lag spike for a second and you didn't hear/saw what was being said/shown to you? And now you need to explain person that you have a problems...\nTo help find answers to these questions and to help handle these situations, I suggest a somewhat idication that marks user as \"is lagging\", which activates by any condition:\n- Local client is not recieving data from other client for more than ~half second, until next portion of data recieved.\n- Local client is recieving non-valid or not properly interpolable or uncommon data from other client for any single frame in last ~5 sec.\n- Local client is detecting whatever other possible internal reasons with other client.\n- Other client set self \"is lagging\" explicity, because had FPS < ~20 for any single frame in last ~5 sec.\n- Other client set self \"is lagging\" explicity, because experiences data/packet loss or (de)serialization problems for any single frame in last ~5 sec.\n- Other client set self \"is lagging\" explicity, because whatever other possible internal reasons.\nIt's important to make this indication operativly updating, at least once per second, to be able to see, feel and confirm issues right now, at current seconds of time.\nNot sure about design. May be do something like bar \"bouncy\" progress bar under nickname, classic spinning \"loading\" circle or color mark.",
